  "layout": "Left-to-right main path: g_host (n_host) -> g_front (n_cmd, n_disp) -> g_cluster (n_warp, n_simd, n_tensor, n_smem) -> g_mem (n_l2, n_mc, n_dram). g_cluster is drawn as one populated template cluster with a 'x4' multiplicity label; the other three clusters are implied by the fan-out from n_disp, not drawn as separate blocks. Inside g_cluster, n_warp sits at the top as the control lane, n_simd and n_tensor in the middle as parallel compute lanes, n_smem at the bottom as the storage lane. g_mem is a horizontal band below the cluster, with n_l2 on the left, n_mc in the middle and n_dram on the right. Reserve a lower corridor for the L2 <-> memory-controller <-> DRAM round trip. Do not expand internal control signals inside the cluster.",
